  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] seeking means to Him through all His names — what the servant knew of them and what he did not know.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وَهَذِه أحب الْوَسَائِل إِلَيْهِ
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  And these #text(fill: luma(120))[\[are\]] the most beloved means #text(fill: luma(120))[\[of approach\]] to Him.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  فَإِنَّهَا وَسِيلَة بصفاته وأفعاله الَّتِي هِيَ مَدْلُول أَسْمَائِهِ
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  For they #text(fill: luma(120))[\[are\]] a means through His attributes and His actions, which #text(fill: luma(120))[\[are\]] the meanings of His names.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وَقَوله أَن تجْعَل الْقُرْآن ربيع قلبِي وَنور صَدْرِي
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  And his saying "that You make the Quran the spring of my heart and the light of my chest" —
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  الرّبيع الْمَطَر الَّذِي يحيي الأَرْض
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  the spring #text(fill: luma(120))[\[means\]] the rain that gives life to the earth.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  شبّه الْقُرْآن بِهِ لحياة الْقُلُوب بِهِ
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  He compared the Quran to it because of the life of hearts through it.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وَكَذَلِكَ شبهه الله بالمطر
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  And likewise, God compared it to the rain.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وَجمع بَين المَاء الَّذِي تحصل بِهِ الْحَيَاة والنور الَّذِي تحصل بِهِ الإضاءة وَالْإِشْرَاق
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  And He combined water — by which life #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] obtained — and light — by which illumination and brightness #text(fill: luma(120))[\[are\]] obtained.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  كَمَا جمع بَينهمَا سُبْحَانَهُ فِي قَوْله
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  Just as He — glorified #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] He — combined them both in His saying:
]

#block(width: 100%, inset: (x: 12pt, y: 6pt), fill: rgb("#f8f6f0"), radius: 3pt, stroke: 0.4pt + luma(220))[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  ﴿أنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَاءِ مَاءً فَسَالَتْ أَوْدِيَةٌ بِقَدَرِهَا فَاحْتَمَلَ السَّيْلُ زَبَدًا رَابِيًا﴾
  #v(0.08cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(40))
  He sent down from the sky water, and valleys flowed according to their measure, and the flood carried rising foam.
  #v(0.06cm)
  #set text(7.5pt, fill: luma(120))
  [13:17] — Sahih Intl: He sends down from the sky, rain, and valleys flow according to their capacity, and the torrent carries a rising foam. And from that [ore] which they heat in the fire, desiring adornments and utensils, is a foam like it. Thus Allah presents [the example of] truth and falsehood. As for the foam, it vanishes, [being] cast off; but as for that which benefits the people, it remains on the earth. Thus does Allah present examples.
]
#v(0.15cm)

#block(width: 100%, inset: (x: 12pt, y: 6pt), fill: rgb("#f8f6f0"), radius: 3pt, stroke: 0.4pt + luma(220))[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  ﴿وَمِمَّا توقدون عَلَيْهِ فِي النَّارِ ابْتِغَاء حلية﴾
  #v(0.08cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(40))
  And from what they heat upon it in the fire seeking ornaments...
  #v(0.06cm)
  #set text(7.5pt, fill: luma(120))
  [13:17]
]
#v(0.15cm)

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وفى قَوْله
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  And in His saying:
]

#block(width: 100%, inset: (x: 12pt, y: 6pt), fill: rgb("#f8f6f0"), radius: 3pt, stroke: 0.4pt + luma(220))[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  ﴿﴿مَثَلُهُمْ كَمَثَلِ الَّذِي اسْتَوْقَدَ نَارًا فَلَمَّا أَضَاءَتْ مَا حَوْلَهُ ذَهَبَ اللَّهُ بِنُورِهِمْ﴾﴾
  #v(0.08cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(40))
  Their example #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] like the example of the one who lit #text(fill: luma(120))[\[a\]] fire, and when it illuminated what #text(fill: luma(120))[\[was\]] around him, God took away their light.
  #v(0.06cm)
  #set text(7.5pt, fill: luma(120))
  [2:17] — Sahih Intl: Their example is that of one who kindled a fire, but when it illuminated what was around him, Allah took away their light and left them in darkness [so] they could not see.
]
#v(0.15cm)

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  ثمَّ قَالَ
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
