  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  and what #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] hated today #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] followed by what #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] loved tomorrow.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  أعظم الرِّبْح فِي الدُّنْيَا أَن تشغل نَفسك كل وَقت بِمَا هُوَ أولى بهَا وأنفع لَهَا فِي معادها
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  The greatest profit in this world #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] that you occupy yourself every moment with what #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] most worthy of it and most beneficial for it in its Return.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  كَيفَ يكون عَاقِلا من بَاعَ الْجنَّة بِمَا فِيهَا بِشَهْوَة سَاعَة
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  How can #text(fill: luma(120))[\[one\]] be rational who sold Paradise with all that #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] in it for #text(fill: luma(120))[\[a\]] moment's desire?
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  يخرج الْعَارِف من الدُّنْيَا وَلم يقْض وطره من شَيْئَيْنِ
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  The knower leaves this world without fulfilling his wish of two things:
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  بكاؤه على نَفسه وثناؤه على ربّه
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
