  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  And with God #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] success.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  ودّع ابْن عون رجلا فَقَالَ عَلَيْك بتقوى الله فَإِن المتقى لَيست عَلَيْهِ وَحْشَة
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  Ibn Awn bade farewell to #text(fill: luma(120))[\[a\]] man and said: 'Hold to God-consciousness, for the God-conscious — #text(fill: luma(120))[\[there\]] is no loneliness upon him.'
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وَقَالَ زيد بن أسلم كَانَ يُقَال من اتَّقى الله أحبه النَّاس وَإِن كَرهُوا
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  And Zayd ibn Aslam said: it used to be said, 'Whoever #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] God-conscious of God, people #text(fill: luma(120))[\[will\]] love him, even if they #text(fill: luma(120))[\[would\]] hate #text(fill: luma(120))[\[to\]].'
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وَقَالَ الثَّوْريّ لِابْنِ أبي ذِئْب إِن اتَّقَيْت الله كَفاك النَّاس
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  And al-Thawri said to Ibn Abi Dhi'b: 'If you are God-conscious of God, #text(fill: luma(120))[\[He will\]] suffice you against people,
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وَإِن اتَّقَيْت النَّاس لن يغنوا عَنْك من الله شَيْئا
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  and if you fear people, they #text(fill: luma(120))[\[will\]] never help you against God #text(fill: luma(120))[\[in\]] anything.'
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وَقَالَ سُلَيْمَان بن دَاوُد أوتينا مِمَّا أُوتِيَ النَّاس وَمِمَّا لم يؤتوا
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  And Sulayman ibn Dawud said: 'We were given from what people were given, and from what they were not given,
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وعلّمنا مِمَّا علّم النَّاس وَمِمَّا لم يعلمُوا
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  and we were taught from what people were taught, and from what they were not taught.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  فَلم نجد شَيْئا أفضل من تقوى الله فِي السِّرّ وَالْعَلَانِيَة
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  And we did not find anything better than God-consciousness in secret and in public,
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
