  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  and envy — and it #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] what made one of the sons of Adam bold against his brother.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  فَمن وقِي شَرّ هَذِه الثَّلَاثَة فقد وقى الشَّرّ
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  So whoever #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] protected from the evil of these three, #text(fill: luma(120))[\[he\]] has been protected from evil.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  فالكفر من الْكبر والمعاصي من الْحِرْص وَالْبَغي وَالظُّلم من الْحَسَد
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  For disbelief #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] from arrogance, sins #text(fill: luma(120))[\[are\]] from greed, and transgression and injustice #text(fill: luma(120))[\[are\]] from envy.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  جعل الله بِحِكْمَتِهِ كل جُزْء من أَجزَاء ابْن آدم ظَاهِرَة وباطنة آلَة لشَيْء
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  God, in His wisdom, made every part of the parts of the son of Adam — outer and inner — #text(fill: luma(120))[\[a\]] tool for something.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  إِذا اسْتعْمل فِيهِ فَهُوَ كَمَاله
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  When it #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] used for #text(fill: luma(120))[\[that purpose\]], then that #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] its perfection.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  فالعين آلَة للنَّظَر وَالْأُذن آلَة للسماع وَالْأنف آلَة للشم
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  The eye #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] #text(fill: luma(120))[\[a\]] tool for seeing, the ear #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] #text(fill: luma(120))[\[a\]] tool for hearing, the nose #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] #text(fill: luma(120))[\[a\]] tool for smelling,
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وَاللِّسَان آلَة للنطق والفرج للنِّكَاح وَالْيَد للبطش وَالرجل للمشي
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  the tongue #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] #text(fill: luma(120))[\[a\]] tool for speech, the private part for marriage, the hand for grasping, and the foot for walking,
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وَالْقلب للتوحيد والمعرفة وَالروح للمحبة
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  the heart for monotheism and knowledge, the spirit for love,
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وَالْعقل آلَة للتفكر والتدبر لعواقب الْأُمُور الدِّينِيَّة والدنيوية
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  and the mind #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] #text(fill: luma(120))[\[a\]] tool for thinking and reflecting on the outcomes of religious and worldly matters,
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وإيثار مَا يَنْبَغِي إيثاره وإهمال مَا يَنْبَغِي إهماله
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  and preferring what should be preferred, and neglecting what should be neglected.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  أخسر النَّاس صَفْقَة من اشْتغل عَن الله بِنَفسِهِ
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  The most losing of people in trade #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] whoever #text(fill: luma(120))[\[was\]] distracted from God by himself,
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  بل أخسر مِنْهُ من اشْتغل عَن نَفسه بِالنَّاسِ
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  rather, more losing than him #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] whoever #text(fill: luma(120))[\[was\]] distracted from himself by people.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  فِي السّنَن من حَدِيث أبي سعيد يرفعهُ
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  In the Sunan, from the hadith of Abu Sa'id, who raised it #text(fill: luma(120))[\[to the Prophet\]]:
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  إِذا أصبح ابْن آدم فَإِن الْأَعْضَاء كلهَا تكفر اللِّسَان
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  "When the son of Adam wakes in the morning, all the limbs humble #text(fill: luma(120))[\[themselves\]] to the tongue,
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  تَقول اتَّقِ الله فَإِنَّمَا نَحن بك
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  saying: 'Fear God, for we #text(fill: luma(120))[\[are\]] only through you.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  فان اسْتَقَمْت استقمنا وَإِن اعوججت اعوججنا
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  If you stand straight, we stand straight, and if you go crooked, we go crooked.'"
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  قَوْله تكفر اللِّسَان قيل مَعْنَاهُ تخضع لَهُ
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  His saying "humble #text(fill: luma(120))[\[themselves\]] to the tongue" — it #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] said its meaning #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]]: they submit to it.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وَفِي الحَدِيث أَن الصَّحَابَة لما دخلُوا على النَّجَاشِيّ لم يكفروا لَهُ
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  And in the hadith, when the Companions entered upon al-Najashi, they did not bow to him —
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  أَي لم يسجدوا وَلم يخضعوا
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  meaning they did not prostrate and did not submit.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وَلذَلِك قَالَ لَهُ عَمْرو بن الْعَاصِ أَيهَا الْملك إِنَّهُم لَا يكفرون لَك
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  And because of that, Amr ibn al-As said to him: 'O king, they do not bow to you.'
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وَإِنَّمَا خضعت للسان لِأَنَّهُ بريد الْقلب وترجمانه والواسطة بَينه وَبَين الْأَعْضَاء
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  And they only submitted to the tongue because it #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] the messenger of the heart and its translator, and the link between it and the limbs.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وَقَوْلها إِنَّمَا نَحن بك أَي نجاتنا بك وهلاكنا بك
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  And their saying 'we #text(fill: luma(120))[\[are\]] only through you' means: our salvation #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] through you, and our destruction #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] through you.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وَلِهَذَا قَالَت فَإِن اسْتَقَمْت استقمنا وَإِن اعوججت اعوججنا
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  And because of this they said: 'If you stand straight, we stand straight, and if you go crooked, we go crooked.'
]
