  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  "O God, I #text(fill: luma(120))[\[am\]] Your servant, #text(fill: luma(120))[\[the\]] son of Your servant, #text(fill: luma(120))[\[the\]] son of Your female servant.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  ناصيتي بِيَدِك مَاض فِيَّ حكمك عدل فِيَّ قضاؤك
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  My forelock #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] in Your hand, Your ruling over me #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] effective, Your decree concerning me #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] just.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  أَسأَلك بِكُل اسْم هُوَ لَك سميت بِهِ نَفسك أَو أنزلته فِي كتابك
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  I ask You by every name that #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] Yours — #text(fill: luma(120))[\[that\]] You named Yourself with, or sent #text(fill: luma(120))[\[it\]] down in Your Book,
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  أَو علّمته أحدا من خلقك أَو استأثرت بِهِ فِي علم الْغَيْب عنْدك
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  or taught #text(fill: luma(120))[\[it to\]] anyone of Your creation, or kept #text(fill: luma(120))[\[it\]] exclusively in the knowledge of the unseen with You —
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  أَن تجْعَل الْقُرْآن ربيع قلبِي وَنور صَدْرِي وجلاء حزني وَذَهَاب همي وغمي
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  that You make the Quran the spring of my heart, the light of my chest, the removal of my sadness, and the departure of my worry and grief."
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  مَا قَالَهَا أحد قطّ إِلَّا أذهب الله همه وغمه وأبدله مَكَانَهُ فرجا
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  No one ever said it except #text(fill: luma(120))[\[that\]] God removed his worry and grief, and replaced #text(fill: luma(120))[\[them\]] in their place #text(fill: luma(120))[\[with\]] relief.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  قَالُوا أَفلا نتعلمهن يَا رَسُول الله
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  They said: "Should we not learn them, O Messenger of God?"
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  قَالَ بلى يَنْبَغِي لمن يسمعهن أَن يتعلمهن
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  He said: "Yes indeed! It #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] fitting for whoever hears them to learn them."
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وَالْمَقْصُود قَوْله عدل فِيَّ قضاؤك
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  And the point #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] his saying: "Your decree concerning me #text(fill: luma(120))[\[is\]] just."
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
  وَهَذَا يتَنَاوَل كل قَضَاء يَقْضِيه على عَبده من عُقُوبَة أَو ألم وَسبب ذَلِك
  #v(0.04cm)
  #set text(dir: ltr, lang: "en", font: "Noto Sans", 9pt, fill: luma(80))
  And this covers every decree He decrees upon His servant — of punishment or pain — and the cause of that.
]

#block(width: 100%, below: 0.2cm)[
  #set text(dir: rtl, lang: "ar", font: "Noto Naskh Arabic", 12pt)
